# Command the vehicle to dive/rise to a target depth.
#
# An action (not a service) because reaching a target depth takes real,
# variable time (seconds to tens of seconds), during which:
#   - the operator benefits from continuous feedback of current depth and
#     distance remaining, rather than an opaque "please wait";
#   - the operator must be able to cancel mid-dive (e.g. abort a descent
#     because a target was reacquired shallower) -- services have no
#     cancellation mechanism, only fire-and-forget or block-until-done.

float64 target_depth
float64 tolerance
---
bool success
float64 final_depth
string message
---
float64 current_depth
float64 distance_remaining
